1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,699
BRAMBLE: Case open!

2
00:00:01,699 --> 00:00:05,014
IVY: Oh no! Our cabin lost its number!

3
00:00:05,214 --> 00:00:07,744
OTTO: Easy! It's number two hundred!

4
00:00:08,144 --> 00:00:11,416
Today's case: a missing house number.

5
00:00:11,716 --> 00:00:15,380
Counting on means saying the next number.

6
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:18,379
It's like a cricket scoreboard.

7
00:00:18,579 --> 00:00:21,642
One more run. One more number.

8
00:00:21,842 --> 00:00:26,226
Ninety-nine, one hundred, one hundred and one.

9
00:00:26,826 --> 00:00:30,081
OTTO: Ninety-nine, one hundred, two hundred!

10
00:00:30,481 --> 00:00:34,091
IVY: Hmm. That cabin says one hundred and one.

11
00:00:34,491 --> 00:00:37,081
BRAMBLE: Let's not guess. Let's test.

12
00:00:37,481 --> 00:00:40,725
BRAMBLE: Can you point to the empty sign?

13
00:00:44,325 --> 00:00:46,552
BRAMBLE: What number goes there?

14
00:00:46,952 --> 00:00:49,219
A. Two hundred.

15
00:00:49,419 --> 00:00:52,067
B. One hundred and two.

16
00:00:52,267 --> 00:00:54,063
Pause and think.

17
00:00:58,663 --> 00:01:01,781
Let's count on from ninety-nine.

18
00:01:01,981 --> 00:01:04,646
Ninety-nine. One hundred.

19
00:01:04,846 --> 00:01:08,524
Past one hundred, keep counting by ones.

20
00:01:08,924 --> 00:01:11,187
One hundred and one.

21
00:01:11,387 --> 00:01:14,060
Then one hundred and two!

22
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:17,788
OTTO: Oh! I jumped way too far!

23
00:01:18,188 --> 00:01:21,224
It's B! One hundred and two.

24
00:01:21,624 --> 00:01:24,619
BRAMBLE: Let's check another way. Count back.

25
00:01:25,019 --> 00:01:29,150
One hundred and four. One hundred and three.

26
00:01:29,350 --> 00:01:31,711
One hundred and two!

27
00:01:32,111 --> 00:01:35,410
IVY: Both ways say one hundred and two!

28
00:01:35,810 --> 00:01:37,078
BRAMBLE: Case solved!

29
00:01:38,578 --> 00:01:41,436
IVY: Look! A snail is moving in!

30
00:01:41,636 --> 00:01:44,079
OTTO: It brought its own house!

31
00:01:44,679 --> 00:01:49,606
Remember. Past one hundred, keep counting by ones.

32
00:01:50,106 --> 00:01:55,320
Say it with me. Past one hundred, keep counting by ones.

33
00:01:57,120 --> 00:02:01,889
Try it at home. Read house numbers on a walk.

34
00:02:02,389 --> 00:02:06,471
Next case: a witness who needs better words.

